1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,408
Forgive me, Father, for I have completely ruined three lives just to chase a hollow dream of absolute power.

2
00:00:09,708 --> 00:00:17,124
The priest behind the wooden screen doesn't offer a gentle prayer. He just lets out a very heavy, tired sigh.

3
00:00:17,424 --> 00:00:26,544
I stole fortunes, wrecked loyal friends, and left a trail of broken promises that nothing can ever truly fix.

4
00:00:26,844 --> 00:00:34,356
You speak of sins as if they belong to someone else, a voice whispers from the dark, cold shadows.

5
00:00:34,656 --> 00:00:43,992
I know every single detail because I lived every single second of that arrogant, selfish, miserable life myself.

6
00:00:44,292 --> 00:00:53,820
The wooden screen slowly slides open, revealing no priest at all, only an older, scarred face staring back.

7
00:00:54,120 --> 00:01:02,928
I am you, aged by decades of endless penance in this exact room, waiting for this exact conversation to end.

8
00:01:03,228 --> 00:01:10,860
There is no absolution here, no clean slate waiting outside. We only trade places to hear the confession again.

9
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:18,672
Now take my seat in the shadows, little me, and prepare to listen to your own endless excuses.

10
00:01:18,972 --> 00:01:23,484
Who will listen when it is your turn to absolve yourself from the trap you built?
